      "name": null,
      "problem": "What are the solutions of the equation $(x-3)^{2}=-9?$",
      "worked_solution": "The left-hand side is a perfect square. Therefore, we can solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-9} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 3\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 3\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=3+3\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=3-3\\,\\text{i}.$",
